# Booking — Recurring Private Reservation Schedules (M23-S04, UC-070)
# TenantContext populated from X-Tenant-ID / X-Actor-ID headers (set by BFF).
# Customer manages their own schedules; STAFF|MANAGER may create on a customer's behalf and see
# every schedule for the tenant (approval queue). Approve/reject (UC-071) are STAFF|MANAGER only.
# A schedule is a fixed term: "endsOn" is required and may not be later than "startsOn" + the
# service's maximum term (Service.bookingPolicy.recurringHorizonDays, 90 days by default) — M23-S18.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run migration:run
#   3. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl    = {{backendUrl}}
@scheduleId = {{requestSchedule.response.body.id}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HAPPY PATH — customer requests a recurring schedule (UC-070 step 1–2)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Request a FIXED_ASSIGNMENT recurring schedule (customer-chosen resource)
# @name requestSchedule
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-29"
}

###

### Request a RESOLVE_PER_OCCURRENCE recurring schedule (system re-resolves each occurrence)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{poolServiceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["monday", "wednesday"],
    "startTime": "08:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "RESOLVE_PER_OCCURRENCE",
  "startsOn": "2026-10-05",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-28"
}

###

### Staff creates a recurring schedule on the customer's behalf
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["thursday"],
    "startTime": "14:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-08",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-31"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# List (customer sees own, STAFF|MANAGER sees all)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### Customer lists their own recurring schedules
GET {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

###

### Customer reads one of their own schedules by id (M23-S42) — the same item as in the list, with
### "serviceName". 404 BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_NOT_FOUND for another customer's schedule or
### another tenant's (a read does not reveal that it exists; ending someone else's stays 403).
GET {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{scheduleId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

###

### Manager reads any schedule of the tenant by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{scheduleId}}
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

###

### Manager lists every recurring schedule for the tenant (first page of 25, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

###

### Manager pages through the approval queue (status filter + limit/offset; limit 1-100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules?status=PENDING_APPROVAL&limit=10&offset=0
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{managerId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: MANAGER

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One occurrence (UC-070 A2) — there is no per-occurrence route: an occurrence is its linked
# booking, so skipping is the ordinary cancel and rescheduling is the ordinary reschedule.
# List a schedule's occurrence bookings with GET /bookings?recurringScheduleId= (bookings.http).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# End (UC-070 A2)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### End the schedule entirely — cancels every future materialized occurrence
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{scheduleId}}/end
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR PATHS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###

### 409 — an occurrence of the term cannot be honored (A1). The body lists EVERY affected one:
# "conflicts": [{ "occurrenceStart": "<ISO-8601 UTC>", "reason": "OCCUPIED" | "CLOSED" | "OUTSIDE_HOURS" }]
# OCCUPIED = an existing booking or hold; CLOSED = a closure or a normally-closed day;
# OUTSIDE_HOURS = outside the business's or the resource's working hours. Nothing is created.
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-29"
}

###

### 409 — the pattern falls outside working hours (reason OUTSIDE_HOURS on every occurrence)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "06:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-29"
}

###

### 409 — the pattern lands on a normally-closed day (a default tenant is closed on Sundays), reason CLOSED
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["sunday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-11",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-27"
}

###

### 422 — endsOn is later than startsOn + the service's maximum term
# BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_TERM_EXCEEDED, params: { "maxTermDays": 90, "latestEndsOn": "2027-01-04" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2027-01-05"
}

###

### 422 — endsOn is before startsOn (BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_INVALID_DATE_RANGE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-09-29"
}

###

### 400 — endsOn is missing (a schedule is never open-ended; request validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06"
}

###

### 422 — service not enabled for recurring reservations
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{nonRecurringServiceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 60
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-06",
  "endsOn": "2026-12-29"
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHERE THE SCHEDULE STARTS (M23-S35) — only the FIRST occurrence meets the booking window
# (tenant settings.booking min/max advance, a service override can only tighten it); later
# occurrences are bounded by the maximum term alone. Nothing is created on any of these.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 422 BOOKING_TOO_SOON — the first occurrence is inside the minimum notice (customer actors only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-13",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-10"
}

###

### 422 BOOKING_TOO_FAR_AHEAD — the first occurrence is beyond the maximum days ahead (customer actors only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2027-06-01",
  "endsOn": "2027-06-29"
}

###

### 422 BOOKING_SCHEDULED_IN_PAST — the first occurrence has already started (staff get this one too)
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["monday","tuesday","wednesday","thursday","friday","saturday","sunday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2020-01-01",
  "endsOn": "2020-01-10"
}

###

### 422 BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_NO_OCCURRENCES — no chosen weekday falls inside the term
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-14",
  "endsOn": "2026-10-14"
}

###

# A renewal: the customer's own previous schedule, the same service/weekdays/time/duration, starting
# no later than the day after that schedule ends. It skips the minimum notice and the maximum days
# ahead, and books only the occurrences that have not started. Anything else is a new schedule.
### Renew the previous schedule — 201 even inside the minimum notice
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-13",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-10",
  "renewsScheduleId": "{{scheduleId}}"
}

###

### 404 BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_NOT_FOUND — renewsScheduleId is unknown, in another tenant, or another customer's
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "{{serviceId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "WEEKLY",
    "daysOfWeek": ["tuesday"],
    "startTime": "10:00",
    "durationMinutes": 120
  },
  "assignmentPolicy": "FIXED_ASSIGNMENT",
  "resourceIds": ["{{resourceId}}"],
  "startsOn": "2026-10-13",
  "endsOn": "2026-11-10",
  "renewsScheduleId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000dead"
}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPROVE / REJECT — staff resolves a PENDING_APPROVAL request (UC-071, M23-S05)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Approve — 200 {id, status: "ACTIVE", occurrenceCount}; every occurrence is materialized APPROVED
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{pendingScheduleId}}/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### Reject — 200 {id, status: "CANCELLED"}; nothing was ever materialized
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{pendingScheduleId}}/reject
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 409 BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_NOT_PENDING_APPROVAL — already approved, rejected or expired
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{scheduleId}}/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 409 BOOKING_RECURRING_SCHEDULE_CONFLICT — a closure or booking appeared while the request waited;
### the body lists every affected occurrence, nothing is created and the request stays pending
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{pendingScheduleWithClosureId}}/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 422 BOOKING_SCHEDULED_IN_PAST — every occurrence of the term started while the request waited;
### occurrences that started are otherwise skipped (never booked). Nothing is created, the request stays pending
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{scheduleId}}/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 404 — unknown schedule
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{staffId}}
X-Actor-Type: STAFF
X-Actor-Role: STAFF

###

### 403 — a customer cannot approve
POST {{baseUrl}}/recurring-booking-schedules/{{pendingScheduleId}}/approve
X-Tenant-ID: {{tenantId}}
X-Actor-ID: {{customerId}}
X-Actor-Type: CUSTOMER
X-Actor-Role: CUSTOMER
